# API controllers

- Package-private `@RestController` + `@RequiredArgsConstructor`.
- Base path: `/api/v1/<plural>` (e.g. `/api/v1/orders`).
- Thin: validate + authorize + call service. No JPA/Redis in controllers.

## HTTP status

| Action | Pattern |
|--------|---------|
| Create | `@ResponseStatus(CREATED)` + `ResponseEntity.created(URI.create(base + "/" + id)).build()` |
| Update/Delete/Read/Auth flows | `@ResponseStatus(OK)` + `void` or DTO body |
| Validation / business errors | throw `app.exception.*` (handler maps status) |

No custom response envelope — return DTOs / `Page<>` directly.

## Security annotations

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Feature permission | `@PreAuthorize("hasAuthority('ORDER_CREATE')")` — names match `GO_PERMISSION` |
| Coarse admin | `@PreAuthorize("hasRole('ADMIN')")` — roles claim gets `ROLE_` prefix |
| Self or admin | `@PreAuthorize("hasRole('ADMIN') or #username == authentication.name")` — see `UserController` |
| Public auth routes | already `permitAll` under `/api/v1/auth/**` — no annotation required |

Do not invent a second permission naming scheme; mirror `ARTICLE_READ|CREATE|UPDATE|DELETE`.

## Paging

- List endpoint: `GET .../paging`
- `@PageableDefault(page = 0, size = 10, sort = "createdAt", direction = DESC)`
- Return `Page<FeatureDTO>`

## Body validation

`@Valid @RequestBody` on write endpoints. Messages live on DTO fields.
